I was having a great game as a wizard the other day.  I found a wand of
wishing on level 2.  I used it to get speed boots, gauntlets of power
(my strength was 6 or something), and +3 Stormbringer (I figured I'd 
could get other weapons by sacrificing).  When I was at exp. level. 4,
I found a like aligned temple priest.  400*4 isn't all that much, so
I suddenly had great armor class.

A few levels later I ran into a bones level with a partially full
treasure zoo.  No problem-o (I think).  I'll just wander in and 
hack and slash.  If I get into trouble, I'll just engrave Elbereth.
I killed almost everything with hardly any damage.  I was invisible,
and the few monsters left seemed to be ignoring me.  So I decided to
eat one of the corpses for intrinsics.  While I'm eating, a nymph 
wakes up, comes over, steals Strombringer, and disappears.

I'm really annoyed.  I start to leave the room to track her down.
On the way out of the room, the "j" I've been ignoring turns out to 
be an ochre jelly and swallows me.  So I was stuck inside the ochre
jelly.  I had:
   - no good weapons (only an athame),
   - no particularly good scrolls (scare monster, remove curse,
     and a few blank ones),
   - rings of invisiblity and regeneration (both being worn),
   - a magic marker and a pick axe,
   - only a few potions (holy water, invisibility),
   - wands of light and slow monster
   - no particularly good spells.
   - speed boots, gauntlets of power, cloak of displacement, and 
     about -12 AC.

I couldn't think of any intelligent way out, so I tried to hack
my way out with the athame.  It seemed to hurt me a lot more than
the jelly, and after about three hits I died.

My question is: did I miss any simple ways out of the jelly?  I suppose
I could've tried to write a teleport spell, but I hadn't seen one yet,
so I didn't think it worth the chance.  Any other suggestions?

